<article class="env-corollary" id="31D86E">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/31D86E">Corollary <span data-tag="31D86E">4.4.4.9</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category, $X$ and object of $\calC $, and $K$ a simplicial set. Let $p: K \rightarrow \calC $ be the constant map taking the value $X$. The objects of the fiber $\calC ^{p/} \times _{\calC } \{ Y\} $ are classified, up to equivalence, by maps $\psi : [K] \rightarrow \bHom _{\calC }(X,Y)$ in the homotopy category $\calH $. Such a map $\psi $ classifies a colimit for $p$ if and only if it induces isomorphisms </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \bHom _{\calC }(Y,Z) \simeq \bHom _{\calC }(X,Z)^{[K]}  \]
</div>
  <p> in the homotopy category $\calH $, for every object $Z$ of $\calC $. </p>
</article>